                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee61077d-3414-3ea9-9566-3d23ea15df1c",
                        "entry_id": "e9579850-6060-3c0f-9471-6f2ea96c0041",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Limber; flexible (either physically or morally)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a995aff3-c2be-4866-958c-6168b89664d2",
                                "sense_id": "ee61077d-3414-3ea9-9566-3d23ea15df1c",
                                "text": "Then the limmer Scottes ared me, burnt my guddes, and made deadlie feede on me and my barnes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71ab7cd2-cb78-438d-8928-56b2147c6c6c",
                                "sense_id": "ee61077d-3414-3ea9-9566-3d23ea15df1c",
                                "text": "The roote is long and very limmer, spreading his bráches both large and long under the earth and doth oftentimes let, hinder, & staye both the plough and Dren in toyling the ground, for they be so tough and limmer, that the share & colter of the plough cannot easily divide and cut them asunder."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6825fc67-7ed8-49ad-bb21-d99f3ab29328",
                                "sense_id": "ee61077d-3414-3ea9-9566-3d23ea15df1c",
                                "text": "Auld plenishen out by was strew'd, Guid L--d but it was limmer; Some creepy stools, an' shelfs weel scower'd Tae hide the worm pict tim'er Tae sell that day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e312f4d9-cdff-4112-a66b-390e07dd33a4",
                                "sense_id": "ee61077d-3414-3ea9-9566-3d23ea15df1c",
                                "text": "If you ride with the hell-spawned reivers and live as a limmer thief then you must expect to be singed by hell's fire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
